<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bovianum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Boiano</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bovianum, modern Boiano in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molise">Molise</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, was the chief town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pentri">Pentri</a>, the largest of the Samnite peoples. It was captured several times by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samnite-wars">Samnite Wars</a> and served as a headquarters of the Italian allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> of 91–88 BCE. It later became a Roman colony.</p></div>
